  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nMarkets showing classic divergence this morning with NASDAQ leading (+1.06%) while DOW lags (-0.15%). VIX spiking to 28.37 (+2.12%) signals elevated anxiety despite the green premarket tape. Iran war headlines dominating the narrative with oil supply concerns front and center.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Initial Jobless Claims (12:30 ET)</strong> - Labor market data could shift Fed expectations if we see significant deviation from consensus</li>\n<li><strong>Retail Sales Control Group (12:30 ET)</strong> - Consumer spending strength will be key given the war's economic drag</li>\n<li><strong>Xi-Trump Summit Development</strong> - Any news on Iran crisis cooperation could spark major moves in energy and risk assets</li>\n<li><strong>Export/Import Price Data (12:30 ET)</strong> - Direct read on inflation pressures from supply chain disruptions</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nRisk-on tech (+0.94%) and growth names leading while defensive utilities (-1.15%) and financials (-1.14%) getting hammered. Real estate (-0.83%) weakness suggests rate cut expectations fading. Energy holding flat despite geopolitical premium - watch for breakout on supply disruption news.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Iran war escalation risk has markets pricing two scenarios: supply shock inflation or demand destruction recession. Energy complex remains the fulcrum.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>VIX above 28 with rates staying elevated crushes multiple expansion. If jobless claims spike, we're looking at stagflation scenario with limited Fed tools.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Diplomatic breakthrough on Iran plus strong retail sales data could trigger short covering rally. Tech leadership suggests growth rotation intact despite macro headwinds.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 740</strong> - Holding this keeps the uptrend alive; break below targets 735 support</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ 720</strong> - Resistance from March highs; clear break signals tech breakout continuation</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 30</strong> - Critical fear level; break above suggests deeper correction coming</li>\n<li><strong>XLE 95</strong> - Energy sector breakout level if geopolitical tensions escalate further</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>"
